hl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What this adds\n\nThe record of the synthetic follow-up and the five natural-text studies (27 Oct – 4 Nov 2026), the adversarial review of their claims, and the response to it. **[`NATURAL_TEXT_STUDIES.md`](NATURAL_TEXT_STUDIES.md) is the index**, and the final claims are in [`RESPONSE.md` §5](reports/adversarial-review-response-20261104-01/RESPONSE.md).\n\n- **248 files**, at their historical relative paths and byte-identical to their local sources (combined SHA-256 of the per-file hash list checked against the laptop copy before committing): sealed source packages and protocols for S, N1, N3, N4 and N5 (N6's are already under `preregistration/` from #3), results, analysis tables (`POINTS.csv`, `FITS.csv`, `ANALYSIS.json`), seed registries, both failure reports, both evidence chains with the superseded-wording note, the review with its recompute scripts and outputs, the response, and the owner's design decisions.\n- **Changed:** `README.md` (two links and one scope sentence), `PUBLICATION_NOTES.md` and `DATA_AVAILABILITY.md` (describe the addition and its one exception), and `PUBLICATION_MANIFEST.csv` (three rows updated in place, 249 appended; the original order and CRLF endings are kept; all 1,185 rows recheck against the files).\n\n## Scope, stated in the index\n\nModels of at most 34.7 M parameters on a 4 GB GPU, with 0.2–2.1 M unique tokens per draw. This is a small-scale methodological study of p\\* under training-progress and learning-rate confounds, **not a replication** of Jane Street's findings. \"Pre-registered\" means hash-sealed locally within one team; only N6 was registered publicly (#3), after its data existed.\n\n## Curation choices to check before merging\n\n- **Owner decisions are included.** `DATA_AVAILABILITY.md` previously excluded approvals. These files are included because the protocols cite them, and because `DECISION.md` (4 Nov) is the correction of record for N1's failure report. They quote messages from the research sessions verbatim. Drop the `reports/natural-text-ladder-owner-decisions-*` folders if you'd rather not publish them.\n- **Excluded:** run folders and anything under `work/runs/`; preparation, probe, seed-package and approval folders; run and engine-check receipts and owner console output; the duplicated analysis rerun in S's result folder; and the battery and power-event records from N3's failure diagnosis.\n- **Checks done:** a scan for personal home paths, emails, machine names and credential patterns found only the public GitHub handle, the noreply commit address and a public SSH commit signature in the PR #3 snapshot. All 85 added Python files parse. Nothing was executed.\n- **Links:** path references inside the added files to excluded material are left as written, to keep the bytes identical.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01JvfaYmnEddgunH3yg39Yo4)_","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T06:03:47Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T06:08:44Z","closed_at":"2026-11-04T06:05:43Z","merged_at":"2026-11-04T06:05:42Z","merge_commit_sha":"332aa76e4c23af72f07501b3f896980fc4c49049","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"rafli-hl:results/natural-text-closure-20261104","ref":"results/natural-text-closure-20261104","repo":{"id":1396932651,"node_id":"R_kgDOU0OAKw","name":"sequence-weighting-research","full_name":"rafli-hl/sequence-weighting-research","owner":{"login":"rafli-hl","id":289911665,"node_id":"U_kgDOEUezcQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289911665?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl","html_url":"https://github.com/rafli-hl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rafli-hl/gist